// PRR, RFC 9937, spreads the window's reduction over the round trip in which the loss shows. The peer has neither
// timestamps nor SACK, so a segment is 1000 bytes and each duplicate ACK stands for one segment the peer holds. Ten
// segments acknowledged one by one double the window to 20000, a write fills it with twenty, and the first is lost.
// A write of 1000 follows every duplicate and shows what the window allows; the send cap is raised to hold them.
//
// Duplicates 1 and 2 each take 1000 out of what is in flight, and one new segment leaves: limited transmit, 22000
// outstanding. Duplicate 3 marks the head lost and recovery begins: the target is 22000 / 2 = 11000, RecoverFS 22000,
// and with 3000 counted received and 1000 lost, 18000 are in flight. Each duplicate from here delivers 1000, and
// while what is in flight is above the target the window is what is in flight plus
// ceil(prr_delivered * 11000 / 22000) - prr_out: half of what was delivered may be sent.
//   3: 500 allowed in all, nothing sent yet: a window of 18500, on which the head is resent whole; a write gets
//      nothing.
//   4: 1000 allowed, 1000 sent: nothing.
//   5 to 16: 500 more at each, and a write sends 500.
//   17: what is in flight has come down to the target, and the conservative bound holds the window there: nothing.
//   18, 19: 10000 in flight, below the target, and the bound lets it back up to 11000: a whole segment each.
// The ACK of everything ends recovery with the window at the target, so a write accepts 11000.
//
// RFC 9937's Figure 1 is this recovery drawn in whole segments, a target of 10 for 20 in flight: one new segment for
// every second duplicate. In bytes the same half is 500 at every duplicate, since writable() offers what the window
// leaves, a part of a segment too. Linux counts whole segments, as the figure does; its reno halves the window, 10
// segments, where RFC 5681 halves the flight, 22, and its PRR divides by the window it had on entry, 20, where RFC
// 9937 divides by RecoverFS.
--congestion=newreno
--tcp_send_segments=64
0 socket(..., SOCK_STREAM, IPPROTO_TCP) = 3
+0 bind(3, ..., ...) = 0
+0 listen(3, 1) = 0

+0 < S 0:0(0) win 65535 <mss 1000>
+0 > S. 0:0(0) ack 1 win 65535 <mss 1460>
+0 < . 1:1(0) ack 1 win 65535
+0 accept(3, ..., ...) = 4

+0 write(4, ..., 20000) = 10000
